          "prompt": "MANDATORY: ONE SINGLE HORIZONTAL ROW of exactly four separate orthographic views of the SAME object, left to right: 1 FRONT view; 2 LEFT side view (object turned so its front points to the LEFT edge of the image); 3 BACK view; 4 RIGHT side view (object turned so its front points to the RIGHT edge of the image). Same scale and same ground line in all four, wide empty gaps between the views, every view complete and not cropped. Pure flat white background. No floor, no ground shadow, no text, no labels, no frames, no perspective, no extra objects.\n\nSTYLE: stylized hand-painted 3D game environment asset painted under even neutral white light with true base colours only: no baked lighting, no cast shadows, no ambient-occlusion darkening, no rim light. Thick chunky simplified silhouette, broad clean faceted planes, two or three dominant colour blocks (ochre-red sandstone, paler sand-yellow strata bands, sand-yellow drift sand), soft painted gradients, sparse medium-size wear. No photorealism, no micro-grain, no fine cracks, no realistic erosion detail, no tiny carvings. Physically plausible.\n\nOBJECT, long low wind-carved boulder (3.6m wide x 1m tall x 1.6m deep): A low, long wind-carved ochre-red sandstone boulder lying on the ground, streamlined by the desert wind like a stone whale back: a blunt rounded head at one end and a long tapering tail at the other. The top is broad and nearly flat; along both long sides run two or three chunky horizontal wind-cut grooves following the rock strata, paler sand-yellow bands between darker ochre-red layers. The base sinks into a low skirt of drifted sand wrapping all around it. FRONT view: the long side, blunt head on the image-LEFT, tail tapering to the image-RIGHT, about 3.6 times as wide as tall. BACK view: the other long side, head on the image-RIGHT. LEFT side view: the tapered tail end, a low rounded hump about 1.6 times as wide as tall. RIGHT side view: the blunt head end, broader and rounder. One solid low cover rock, no loose pebbles.",
